<p>ALERT ALERT: INEXPERIENCED CRITIQUE</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">By&nbsp;clicking&nbsp;me,&nbsp;you&nbsp;are&nbsp;aware&nbsp;I'm&nbsp;bad&nbsp;at&nbsp;critting&nbsp;and&nbsp;cannot&nbsp;give&nbsp;greenlights</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">HEY,&nbsp;don't&nbsp;click&nbsp;that&nbsp;hard&nbsp;next&nbsp;time</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>All right, first off, it sort of feels like this is a copy pasta from a draft. If so, this is not recommended, as said in the required reading (I think). If this is not a copy pasta, ignore this.</p>
<p>I'm an avid fan of the foundation, but I have no idea what a &quot;Phycological Physical Mutation&quot; is. This kind of language is good for articles, but confusing for drafts. People shouldn't have to look up what words mean in a draft. I also suggest putting in parenthesis what NOAA stands for.</p>
<p>About the elevator pitch. It is meant to explain the anomaly. All I know from it is that its a big, dark, 4 legged, water thing that doesn't like being seem. Maybe add some more description about what it does there.</p>
<p>Your central narrative is about the story of the SCP, which, with what it says in its current state, implies its all about how the foundation captured it. Regardless, the foundation is smart with its resources, so why would it repeatedly send people in on suicide missions? Surely they would provide them with the ability to counteract its properties. This, with the mention of an MTF, seems like the foundation throwing d class at it until it shuts up, on a bigger scale.</p>
<p>Putting that aside, after the second fail, why don't the foundation just try to contain it in the ocean? They are powerful enough to build a containment cell underwater with the capabilities similar to those on land. Though the, &quot;block off all interaction from it&quot; route could work, it would relate it too much to <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-169">SCP-169 &quot;The Leviathan&quot;</a></p>
<p>Final note, I don't do re-crits, fyi</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Enjoy the crit, angryman, awaaay&#8230;</p>

