<p>Requested by PM so lets see what I can do here for ya.</p>
<p>So looking at this SCP here, it seems almost overly complex. You describe what it looks like, but not how it does anything listed. Do the seven pupils serve a purpose or are they just there for aesthetic? And while most forms of saved images are ill advised, how do we know what the creature looks like with such detail from less than one minute viewings? I also am confused about the fauna transforming, did the SCP do that? If so, why did it do that and how? I would try and outline some more of these things so that reader has key information about the SCP rather than just what it looks like.</p>
<p>As for the narrative, I don't see much of one attached. I see you mention failed containment attempts, will they be apart of the article? The major thing I would try and tweak is it's discovery. Increased saltiness in the water? Concerning, yes. Foundation threat, no. Perhaps after initial NOAA investigation, there were reports of hostile fauna or the like thus triggering involvement. I am also rather bugged about the site you refer to as &quot;the ring&quot; I have no idea what this is, or why it holds significance. If you mean just another site, try Site-xxx. It's more formal and fits the article format better. Best of luck.</p>

